    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0518" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1391.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 2024, of the 5th instant,
                    relating” to the defilement of the coat of arms of the United States at the
                    consulate in Bamberg, has been received.</p>
                <p>The Department is gratified at the friendly spirit shown by the Government of
                    Germany in regretting the incident and in bringing it about that the new coat of
                    arms will be put in place in a solemn manner.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
